{"title":"Spencer’s Favorite Bikes of Grit Fest 2026 – Spencer Harding","link":"https://theradavist.com/spencers-favorite-bikes-of-grit-fest-2026","date":1794294593000,"content":"<p><em>While attending this year’s new and rejuvenated Grit Fest, an inclusive bike festival hosted by <a href=\"https://allbikeswelcome.org/\" target=\"_blank\">All Bikes Welcome</a>, Spencer picked a few of his favorite bikes from the crowd to document. He hit every wheel size, so no nerd will feel left out. Check what he found below…</em></p>\n<p><span></span></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/409d0e0adf08accbd18a7a089cd64360b48708bc91772910f07dc8a042a0b596.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/20e1096514f54791dc343d30bf05ef2302bb9c84d1a3f31defdbee6b16141471.jpg 800w, /media/409d0e0adf08accbd18a7a089cd64360b48708bc91772910f07dc8a042a0b596.jpg 1600w, /media/ed794eb720e353027e4628e0e08c66378c319509f0d026f0ac9755da25ff6cd7.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/b2f329531e2b642f9399d890bbb395238bfbb17f7d7aba16c0e876d3281c3217.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/f75c1e9276aef4e4423dc4b6891478e6a9c9298a89eb3dc388430f9cbc667f8f.jpg 800w, /media/b2f329531e2b642f9399d890bbb395238bfbb17f7d7aba16c0e876d3281c3217.jpg 1600w, /media/c39179367dafe087d020fd2a338107750ca0a74e0e9b040a3544f890a0721b5b.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/91b319a77ded63a80da58f78f4616bad8e23e94467b862cea954b5eb4b114db8.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/d555ed96c8f5dbde051478d5e1fdef2b9802bba598ebc3339484d7845c23a22d.jpg 800w, /media/91b319a77ded63a80da58f78f4616bad8e23e94467b862cea954b5eb4b114db8.jpg 1600w, /media/ac71d51de1f5baa3506f2823711a96389f775c47ba299b4c9aa3defda10f5879.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Much like my coverage at Bike Camp earlier this year, I couldn’t fit the bike check in with all the coverage of the event, so you’re getting two whole articles. I have three bikes for your consideration, hailing from decades ago to a few months old, across the spectrum of wheel sizes, 26″-29″; all you 32″ haters can breathe a sigh of relief. Check out my favorite bikes from the Grit Fest weekend and the equally lovely humans who built and pedaled them.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/957fad89843edf345f802413a0cfac19a8880a5d6bb95aca5a278e2e97830ec7.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/0d216fc7a0eb5f51a10c5106eee524be7eeed54ba20aa2a272cf2bb423f4d08c.jpg 640w, /media/957fad89843edf345f802413a0cfac19a8880a5d6bb95aca5a278e2e97830ec7.jpg 1800w, /media/ba95c40532a16daaf2fd2db9baef1d691f8e7dca32952c90ee3495112def94a1.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3>Reese’s <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/tag/gary-fisher\" target=\"_blank\">Gary Fisher</a> Hoo Koo E Koo</h3>\n<p>Details, details, details, Reese’s bike begged closer inspection. With the rear brake posts chopped and re-welded for 650b, this Hoo Koo E Koo isn’t like the others.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/c83592d4302665b50595bef28d89c0b89921abd7c6410343fc0260c399952596.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/f634b1ee793d04e51aa650ecb4a80cb7531d06dfb06aab57cd3acf749e9d16b9.jpg 800w, /media/c83592d4302665b50595bef28d89c0b89921abd7c6410343fc0260c399952596.jpg 1600w, /media/7797c64200447150bf5e8eba100715257ca3d4fc7bfeae58655493383a9979d0.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/7b38cfb33d1bd0da1706d50811c8ea7db1a56e2c3a41a5034ffb22d8f7f88b2d.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/87f10540962408721e18489a1a4954b58a39664f2f4bc631f25c2f4e24048634.jpg 800w, /media/7b38cfb33d1bd0da1706d50811c8ea7db1a56e2c3a41a5034ffb22d8f7f88b2d.jpg 1600w, /media/8962b210060805e27403d4124107ebc6e2940293f9879820c59e097830cffc55.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/fcb143be9479a3f65897c949ff5a16d5a65f14e812c8d633cabf6d7baa176b75.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/af18d517ecd76e1c3929412bb53ebce994cf8a7423846fb0e48d4fb610b308a2.jpg 800w, /media/fcb143be9479a3f65897c949ff5a16d5a65f14e812c8d633cabf6d7baa176b75.jpg 1600w, /media/8cacff60a751d5edbc62fc6d8a758741a8d6f22de695f23a067675389c5a5db1.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Reese’s spare chain fashion bleeds into the build with a mismatched chain as well as a Deore XT lower cage hacked onto an XTR parallelogram. The hacking doesn’t stop there with her custom decauleur. The topo designs framebag perfectly mirrors the Velo Orange rack by becoming a mini pannier.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/7680c6d4998ef0e17c6243abcb34790f6686d1cfde1935c5ac2e67ff3175870c.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/9fa0ea07116116fce41f656bc53654caa94f0165e18a9543d3167a8199865720.jpg 800w, /media/60cac4ced81426f372ee5581653dd94cefa4d85075736528e94dde4b07499c4a.jpg 1600w, /media/7680c6d4998ef0e17c6243abcb34790f6686d1cfde1935c5ac2e67ff3175870c.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/0cdd2dd2d24eb5d946894b0649fd661e9d3cccc0e93c56bc7bd079448eda3ca4.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/3d9ff28fefe2dec773d5a322b1bf4f0b5164a5beef97edb2c7b47f92e94c638a.jpg 800w, /media/aa3dafd6118e86389fad0300c5218ad4832cf61c92e80523b5d3d751af2fe461.jpg 1600w, /media/0cdd2dd2d24eb5d946894b0649fd661e9d3cccc0e93c56bc7bd079448eda3ca4.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Purple anodized bits from Paul, Chris King, and Sim Works permeate the build, adding pops of color. I really love the faded ano on the Chris King hubs with an asymmetrical lacing pattern: 2x drive side, straight non-drive side.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/146f5774910824825f1099a205820776384cc7921687c0c7d561f11242af9104.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/7628f6858c7c554f950fd4877e32ac89734e1951afebbe3a1a937f8f3a15c702.jpg 640w, /media/146f5774910824825f1099a205820776384cc7921687c0c7d561f11242af9104.jpg 1800w, /media/f7dfc3e60fb371cd64f2376ed78abd1d757d1ba3d416a3668a96287ab292f797.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>With so many details and non part left unexamined, Reese’s Gary Fisher was an absolute favorite of the weekend at Grit Fest.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/4a1865450173efc6c435d9768c2ebd7d618e2efe5718d438432dfc388e7613b6.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/7299caec793da6be2ca8f8b939b2658e8f672551e69c892116e1e1da50abe42f.jpg 640w, /media/4a1865450173efc6c435d9768c2ebd7d618e2efe5718d438432dfc388e7613b6.jpg 1800w, /media/1f6b25f258229b312429e01cad5af168dd21773ef201e76e75bb80f5e9e41b0f.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3>Dan’s Personal <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/tag/pachyderm\" target=\"_blank\">Pachyderm</a> “Truck Bike”</h3>\n<p>Moving on to the most modern and largest-wheeled bike of my picks with Dan’s Pachyderm. Only after shooting this bike did I learn that Dan was the builder and sole proprietor of Pachyderm bikes. Dan’s personal rig is a slacked-out rigid 29er with a custom stainless steel front rack. Here is the geo if you wanna nerd out about it with Dan:</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/4dd964c7eeea6ad8aa92690770d7523d9862e9c74755278e95d635595a4559b6.png\" srcset=\"/media/ed64ca31ec11d5940fd1137180c46b65dc93e8ec8fae4d3ae94d2cb098c649a5.png 640w, /media/4dd964c7eeea6ad8aa92690770d7523d9862e9c74755278e95d635595a4559b6.png 1800w, /media/9551a9089cb1ead957d60af36100d331b331433330ee55b40d90904d271e62a9.png\" /></p>\n<p>Initially, the Type-2-inspired fork caught my eye, but the overall stance and nice lines held my interest. The fork was made from “some old Columbus 26 in unicrown blades matched to straight gauge 1-1/8 in blades.” With a mismatched Boost front hub and standard 142mm rear hub (what he already had), mated to a 73mm BB, this bike is truly custom. The stand-off bosses on the seat tube allow for lots of dropper post insertion. The color is “frosted shamrock” sprayed by Blue City Cycles, an old shop mate of Dan’s from Chicago.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/d07720c48155c8a613c2980559391090b7db0289e42b82e7ac9830857336dcd4.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/502f68b314a9a64d30f822b53976ae1ae1968a89c13b95553eb9670fa8352129.jpg 800w, /media/5ee555cb8cdf647885c77cb7eceda727e896621f1dcc1d25d17d72a64b7b3f69.jpg 1600w, /media/d07720c48155c8a613c2980559391090b7db0289e42b82e7ac9830857336dcd4.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/83cbddeff0c0b2b0507ea19e8e45d7e3053172a886f7d566ce06df9adf44cd0e.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/f8b849d9bc159dac88a38dc94744015689adb831cd3b444b1b4a10ef777f525a.jpg 800w, /media/94d65d8212e04d88c0e546a45a79f37fca9a0f8f8f42e84c6f362c8958315792.jpg 1600w, /media/83cbddeff0c0b2b0507ea19e8e45d7e3053172a886f7d566ce06df9adf44cd0e.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Featuring a cable-actuated connoisseur’s groupo with SRAM XX1 11-speed drivetrain, Paul Klamper stoppers. The Chicago crew really had a hankering for purple anodized bits, though Dan went less ostentatious than Reese with just some purple valve stems.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/af577b5208dcfd649d27ea558c775113f12bd7adf974c75ccae72cd6a80dc82d.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/a9a85ffd0cc489f871302abc0c460708162d5cddbcdf465a52f734f367b729c6.jpg 640w, /media/af577b5208dcfd649d27ea558c775113f12bd7adf974c75ccae72cd6a80dc82d.jpg 1800w, /media/6ec6ffa473a5ca11621f675295444baa06591428bdc4caa0fbaa667045aaf1d6.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Dan’s rowdy rigid Pachyderms was perfectly suited for our longer single track laden ride on Sunday. Looked like a hoot and I can’t wait to make it out to Chicago and check out his shop and the rest of the Bubbly Dynamics freambuilding collective.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/e090237332917bcc236757f7f0e667c3dac4f15066acb13a9306719d8a0228e2.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/26044317abaf8cc025774a88eeff2dc57e82b5a9c2ba5fcaaae35505503304c4.jpg 640w, /media/e090237332917bcc236757f7f0e667c3dac4f15066acb13a9306719d8a0228e2.jpg 1800w, /media/633f61809ddec3e3a121106c2d95b691d6a1a3a4ab01713e825c204138faa3d4.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3>Mer’s <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/tag/dean-bikes\" target=\"_blank\">Dean</a> Titanium</h3>\n<p>In an effort to appease the vintage 26er restomod mafia, I hereby present Mer’s 26er Dean Titanium.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/94940bc8711ff3f6e9b5c44eddb5bf76f5b8ed22360265e9c7d423423097065a.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/0a0ac2558049063e27de875e6bf868401280e227ba06422a73982b2a7b3818b1.jpg 800w, /media/a00add3d61a38a4440388f3cc8bbaae71cde0eaa3ccc4a1ceda41bf547af26e3.jpg 1600w, /media/94940bc8711ff3f6e9b5c44eddb5bf76f5b8ed22360265e9c7d423423097065a.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/8c6a77962eb7777438f402ac78533740c1ee463f6e6b710527388d79d818cd65.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/2db5be6b7b3d3b168da3dd09bebc3236b393299612f1e479ec453cfab1cb08e4.jpg 800w, /media/8c8f84468fdc059ad124dca67adf9a86583a04a9a9a4439a95648a373c66a835.jpg 1600w, /media/8c6a77962eb7777438f402ac78533740c1ee463f6e6b710527388d79d818cd65.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Sky-high bullmoose bars, check.</p>\n<p>Headset pipe, check.</p>\n<p>XTR hubs, check.</p>\n<p>Matching Realm TT pad and water bottle, big check.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/0f8da9007df6457f657dfde2396a868f5d87c1c92c7b3c3fcd5d9ef5c3c39719.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/3144efb11c22ced153c38bdba6261d73295fb06c63393dbcf9f52242783f784c.jpg 800w, /media/0f8da9007df6457f657dfde2396a868f5d87c1c92c7b3c3fcd5d9ef5c3c39719.jpg 1600w, /media/8f88bc6f96603c87224d8fd390dcc3cd1c5236ac83712df2c89299351a062a26.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/a880eaec359f88e79d7d959efc96aada05242a4a4c503ff93980256f49269cc8.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/4036696546e2ef13b43292c79dd78dba755d6cb21e678362b1ba196d53f834b3.jpg 800w, /media/a880eaec359f88e79d7d959efc96aada05242a4a4c503ff93980256f49269cc8.jpg 1600w, /media/9098724613003be2c864a3ea6f8d5ae03cecad0e11f4531c7b187d1e252fdc31.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/b5772181da490ef4e7cc38cf4f7a144269cdcdae0f3c2de5077586f823c91973.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/b9ff203882a65a4cb9f44672314e2a9a129fc49a51a9333e29f20223a90c059d.jpg 800w, /media/b5772181da490ef4e7cc38cf4f7a144269cdcdae0f3c2de5077586f823c91973.jpg 1600w, /media/fc19430918a1e9ac399b9f55f8dd3f37aef70fe0429df14774093a22f61b091a.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>I got to watch Mer take this comfort shred sled out for a night ride around the techy trails of Lake Leatherwood. Undeterred by the small wheels, we were successful in our mission, if not covered in a few cobwebs. Mer has the distinction of being an outlier with the Paul 100% cranks, but they are at least square taper; we’re still in spec, y’all. The Avid Single Digit brake arms perfectly matching the raw Ti sheen was *chef kiss*.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/fc3b373d67047d7c846dce33020373ecf378e94a34114cc67d72512fd8651822.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/a8128999605f2df0e0a401a72a39227a588e274134c04e0b89e6f5aa23b98c36.jpg 640w, /media/fc3b373d67047d7c846dce33020373ecf378e94a34114cc67d72512fd8651822.jpg 1800w, /media/a22917b3a7996dda6335d3997c3e22172744df29e44dbbcfe648d5e9c7d7a23b.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Well done Mer, it was a pleasure to pedal around with you at Grit Fest.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/4b4b73ebd768651774241164e81f69690b54e3fc640d07cda8ad39d7f7d806d7.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/fecaf9ae2df4f50e8fc1a728b952f594a92969c7795503439bd737b90ad8b903.jpg 800w, /media/4b4b73ebd768651774241164e81f69690b54e3fc640d07cda8ad39d7f7d806d7.jpg 1600w, /media/8b35f90b084200f3d9f4a4cb1a11b37845ab22185842d04a1bb539f6f4fbc94d.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/08f45d70d79bd10370d1b2fa8a874b71866c8e1c3923b3743db475db39f4d4d7.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/c3ecf9f904e2354eb69e1b8a19e7dd5e72b8fd240ab6ae41205072790cb09342.jpg 800w, /media/08f45d70d79bd10370d1b2fa8a874b71866c8e1c3923b3743db475db39f4d4d7.jpg 1600w, /media/4dd22a52b6c7f590c077dd815e0b91705998bfddf709288232336bad2eed3c43.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/312ebd8f31c4589e8eb975b20570519fa29eae97e460bab7d412e00421805c24.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/3a97157efe677beeb45df6374ea74145ebf42a0ef874207d21784d1cc785ba12.jpg 800w, /media/312ebd8f31c4589e8eb975b20570519fa29eae97e460bab7d412e00421805c24.jpg 1600w, /media/542842b8c34e4b854f5abdcf1039193f88fab42533960268945cb354ed9556d9.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3>Honorable Mentions</h3>\n<p>There were plenty of amazing bikes at Grit Fest, this is but a small vignette. I figured I should include a few honorable mentions: the Courtney Cox-signed Schwinn, the streamers and cat loving basket bike, and Dr. J Maniac’s Tostitos scooter.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/spencers-favorite-bikes-of-grit-fest-2026\">Spencer’s Favorite Bikes of Grit Fest 2026</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://cms.theradavist.com/\">The Radavist</a>.</p>","author":"spencer harding","comments":"https://theradavist.com/spencers-favorite-bikes-of-grit-fest-2026#comments","siteTitle":"The Radavist","siteHash":"96eb481d8084f04a4602bac57874ba717baf56b758f45547b5caf2312da766ef","entryHash":"7719009dbfa597abe626cf921f7c4cb28ad44285e17885c7517bf883d231ab2e","category":"Cycling"}